description:
Italian, 17th/19th century
Group of 15 Cameos and Intaglios

agate, mounted on a later hardstone plaque, within a later gilt bronze frame with Bourbon iconography

Incorporating (left to right by row from the top):

An Italian 19th-century agate cameo with the head of a young woman;

An Italian 19th-century agate cameo with the head of a warrior;

An Italian 19th-century agate cameo with the head of Jupiter;

Two agate intaglios with equestrian subjects in antique style;

An Italian possibly 19th-century carnelian intaglio with a portrait, set on an associated aventurine glass plaque;

An Italian 16th-century agate cameo with the bust of a man;

An Italian 19th-century cameo with the head of a woman;

An Italian possibly 17th-century cameo with the head of a woman;

An agate intaglio with an animal subject in antique style;

An Italian 19th-century agate cameo with Vespasian;

An Italian possibly 19th-century carnelian intaglio with the head of a man;

An Italian 19th-century sardonyx intaglio with the head of a woman;

An Italian 19th-century agate cameo with the head of a man;

An Italian 19th-century agate cameo with a helmeted warrior

frame: 29 by 18cm., 11⅜ by 7⅛in.

